# ---- Website ----
web.tagline = 2D chat with your own avatars and rooms
web.enter = Open the chat
web.nav.features = Features
web.nav.howto = Getting started
web.nav.safety = Safety
web.nav.legal = Legal
web.hero.text = A chat that looks like a place. You move through rooms as a picture, speak in bubbles and set everything up yourself – in the browser, no installation.
web.f.avatars.h = Your own avatars
web.f.avatars.p = Upload pictures, cut them out and wear up to twelve at once. Everything goes into your bag and stays there.
web.f.rooms.h = Rooms and doors
web.f.rooms.p = Your own rooms with your own background, connected by doors. Lock your room with a single click if you like.
web.f.guilds.h = Guilds and clans
web.f.guilds.p = Found a group, define your own rank names and rights, earn renown and unlock benefits with it.
web.f.media.h = Watch together
web.f.media.p = Share a video in the room – it plays for everyone at once. Prefer listening only? Switch to audio.
web.f.whisper.h = Whispers and group chat
web.f.whisper.p = Private messages even across rooms, plus a channel only group members can read.
web.f.script.h = Program your rooms
web.f.script.p = With PPScript rooms react to events – greet, count, forward. One line, one command.
web.howto.h = Three steps to join
web.howto.1 = Tap “Open the chat”. As a guest you get a name right away – nothing else needed.
web.howto.2 = Put a picture into your bag as an avatar and wear it.
web.howto.3 = For your own rooms or a guild, become a member. Your name is then reserved for you.
web.safety.h = How moderation works here
web.safety.filter = Moderation is mostly automatic: filters catch blocked words, flooding and suspicious content. The use of automated methods including AI is possible but is currently not taking place.
web.safety.noread = Nobody simply reads along. Conversations are not permanently observed. Logs are looked at only for a reason – after a report or on concrete suspicion.
web.safety.logged = To make that possible, rooms are logged. The notice “moderated & logged” is permanently visible in the chat window.
web.safety.own = Participation is at your own responsibility. Content comes from the users, not from the operator.
web.safety.report = Report problems: use ::page to reach moderation directly in the chat.
web.legal.imprint = Imprint
web.legal.privacy = Privacy
web.legal.terms = Terms of use
web.status = Status
web.footer.note = Privately run hobby project. No guarantee of availability.

